{
  "schema": 1,
  "id": "bug-interval-boundaries",
  "category": "brownfield-bug-fix",
  "title": "Exclusive interval endpoints are incorrectly included",
  "request": "Fix inWindow(value, {min, max, minInclusive, maxInclusive}) in src/interval.mjs. Both endpoint flags default to true; a false flag excludes exactly that endpoint. Equal bounds contain the value only when both flags are true. Keep refusal of nonfinite numbers and reversed bounds. Do not change the check.",
  "seededFailure": "The implementation ignores both inclusive flags. The visible check names an excluded lower bound; fixing only that side leaves the upper-bound behavior wrong. A lower-only shortcut is graded independently.",
